+++ b/specs/005-create-patch/spec.md
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# Feature: createPatch (diff as JSON Patch)
+
+Standard: RFC 6902 sections 4.1 (add), 4.2 (remove), 4.3 (replace); paths per RFC 6901 section 3/4 (escaping `~0`, `~1`).
+
+- `createPatch(from, to)` returns a JSON Patch that `applyPatch(from, patch)` turns into `to`.
+- Minimal: objects are compared member by member; arrays by longest common subsequence, so insertion/deletion
+  is one `add`/`remove`, and a move is a `remove` + `add`; changed items in the same slot are diffed in depth.
+- Equal documents (JSON equality, member order irrelevant) give `[]`. Differing types or scalars give `replace`
+  (path `""` for the root).
+- Inputs are not mutated; patch values are copies. `__proto__` keys are plain members.
+- Tests: `tests/create-patch.test.ts` (written with the feature, includes randomized round-trip).
